    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "The route changes · 1 · preparation 2",
    "context": "Use this subset of the travel vocabulary and constructions in a short self-contained situation, preparing for U5-16. Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to choose a route after a disruption and explain how to reach the destination.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-16-P02-speak-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-16-P02-speak-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "The route changes · 1 · preparation 2: Present a supported viewpoint about the decision in this account. Refer to a concrete source detail, acknowledge a plausible alternative, and qualify what the evidence cannot establish.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "我第一次到这座城市，要在火车站和朋友见面。他发来消息，让我在站台上走到前面的出口。我看着手机，却不清楚前面指哪边。\n\n我没有随便往一个方向走，而是先告诉朋友自己下车时站在哪里。他这才明白，我们面对的方向不一样，说的前面也可能是两个不同的地方。\n\n他重新说明，让我往能看到大门的那一边走，再经过旁边的台阶。这样说以后，我可以把消息和眼前的东西联系起来。\n\n到了台阶附近，我停下来仔细看，没有急着离开站台。朋友又发来出口旁边的照片，我对着照片找到了那家商店，才确认自己走对了。\n\n见面以后，我把这段经过讲给他听。他说自己天天走这条路，觉得很容易，忘了第一次来的人不知道他平时习惯站在哪里。\n\n我们约好以后说明要走的路时，应该说清楚能看见的地方。熟悉的人觉得很容易理解的方向，对第一次来的人却可能需要更多清楚的信息。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "A concrete source detail supports my position."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I represented the alternative fairly and retained an important qualification."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
